    },
    "RTOG 90-05" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "RTOG 90-05"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "RTOG 90-05 が最大径 20 mm 以下に定めた最大耐容線量。対象は再発・既照射例" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The maximum tolerated dose defined by RTOG 90-05 for tumors 20 mm or less in maximum diameter. The trial population was recurrent, previously irradiated tumors."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Rich/Chow 2018 メタ解析" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rich/Chow 2018 meta-analysis"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Rx は処方線量、Dmax は最大線量、Dx% は標的の x% が受ける線量です。\nどちらも値が小さいほど均一で、RTOG 型は 1、ICRU-83 型は 0 が下限です。\nSBRT では意図的に標的内を不均一にするため、値が大きいことが\nただちに問題を意味するわけではありません。" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rx is the prescription dose, Dmax the maximum dose, and Dx% the dose received by x% of the target.\nFor both indices a smaller value means greater homogeneity; the lower bound is 1 for the RTOG form and 0 for the ICRU-83 form.\nSBRT deliberately makes the dose inside the target inhomogeneous, so a large value does not\nby itself indicate a problem."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "SBRT（体幹部）" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "SBRT (body)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "SRT（頭蓋内）" : {
