      }
    },
    "TROG SRS Technical Working Group (2026)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "TROG SRS Technical Working Group (2026)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TV は標的体積（PTV）、PIV は処方線量以上を受ける全体積、\nTV_PIV は PTV のうち処方線量以上を受ける体積です。\nRTOG 型は標的外への広がりを区別できませんが、Paddick 型は\n標的の被覆不足と標的外への漏れの両方を反映します。" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "TV is the target volume (PTV), PIV the total volume receiving at least the prescription dose, and\nTV_PIV the part of the PTV receiving at least the prescription dose.\nThe RTOG form cannot distinguish spill outside the target, whereas the Paddick form\nreflects both under-coverage of the target and spill outside it."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "V50%" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "V50%"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "V50%Rx は処方線量の 50% 以上を受ける体積です。\nいずれも標的の外側で線量がどれだけ速く落ちるかを表し、\n値が小さいほど勾配が急です。\n\nR50% と D2cm は RTOG 0813 / 0915 が PTV 体積ごとの許容値を定めています。\n本アプリの逸脱判定はその表を参照するもので、推奨や指示ではありません。" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "V50%Rx is the volume receiving at least 50% of the prescription dose.\nAll of these describe how quickly the dose falls off outside the target;\na smaller value means a steeper gradient.\n\nRTOG 0813 / 0915 define tolerance values for R50% and D2cm by PTV volume.\nThe deviation assessment in this app refers to those tables; it is not a recommendation or an instruction."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Whelan 2010 (OCOG)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Whelan 2010 (OCOG)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
